{"schema":"SDW_SCRIPTURE_CHAPTER_V1","revision":"52add6f41edc5dd9c21f65f02f933fbd1cec266285bee8bce249607475050398","canonicalSourceHash":"f9dfbce6dd2edfe4bb3b4690acd6622f392035be2b0349df98f3607f0a05f6c2","bookId":"engwebu:pro","chapter":31,"verses":[{"translation_id":"engwebu","book_id":"engwebu:pro","chapter":31,"verse_ordinal":885,"verse_start":1,"verse_end":1,"verse_label":"1","text":"The words of King Lemuel—the revelation which his mother taught him:","is_omitted":0,"source_line":2811},{"translation_id":"engwebu","book_id":"engwebu:pro","chapter":31,"verse_ordinal":886,"verse_start":2,"verse_end":2,"verse_label":"2","text":"“Oh, my son! Oh, son of my womb! Oh, son of my vows!","is_omitted":0,"source_line":2814},{"translation_id":"engwebu","book_id":"engwebu:pro","chapter":31,"verse_ordinal":887,"verse_start":3,"verse_end":3,"verse_label":"3","text":"Don’t give your strength to women, nor your ways to that which destroys kings.","is_omitted":0,"source_line":2818},{"translation_id":"engwebu","book_id":"engwebu:pro","chapter":31,"verse_ordinal":888,"verse_start":4,"verse_end":4,"verse_label":"4","text":"It is not for kings, Lemuel, it is not for kings to drink wine, nor for princes to say, ‘Where is strong drink?’","is_omitted":0,"source_line":2821},{"translation_id":"engwebu","book_id":"engwebu:pro","chapter":31,"verse_ordinal":889,"verse_start":5,"verse_end":5,"verse_label":"5","text":"lest they drink, and forget the law, and pervert the justice due to anyone who is afflicted.","is_omitted":0,"source_line":2825},{"translation_id":"engwebu","book_id":"engwebu:pro","chapter":31,"verse_ordinal":890,"verse_start":6,"verse_end":6,"verse_label":"6","text":"Give strong drink to him who is ready to perish, and wine to the bitter in soul.","is_omitted":0,"source_line":2828},{"translation_id":"engwebu","book_id":"engwebu:pro","chapter":31,"verse_ordinal":891,"verse_start":7,"verse_end":7,"verse_label":"7","text":"Let him drink, and forget his poverty, and remember his misery no more.","is_omitted":0,"source_line":2831},{"translation_id":"engwebu","book_id":"engwebu:pro","chapter":31,"verse_ordinal":892,"verse_start":8,"verse_end":8,"verse_label":"8","text":"Open your mouth for the mute, in the cause of all who are left desolate.","is_omitted":0,"source_line":2834},{"translation_id":"engwebu","book_id":"engwebu:pro","chapter":31,"verse_ordinal":893,"verse_start":9,"verse_end":9,"verse_label":"9","text":"Open your mouth, judge righteously, and serve justice to the poor and needy.”","is_omitted":0,"source_line":2837},{"translation_id":"engwebu","book_id":"engwebu:pro","chapter":31,"verse_ordinal":894,"verse_start":10,"verse_end":10,"verse_label":"10","text":"Who can find a worthy woman? For her value is far above rubies.","is_omitted":0,"source_line":2841},{"translation_id":"engwebu","book_id":"engwebu:pro","chapter":31,"verse_ordinal":895,"verse_start":11,"verse_end":11,"verse_label":"11","text":"The heart of her husband trusts in her. He shall have no lack of gain.","is_omitted":0,"source_line":2844},{"translation_id":"engwebu","book_id":"engwebu:pro","chapter":31,"verse_ordinal":896,"verse_start":12,"verse_end":12,"verse_label":"12","text":"She does him good, and not harm, all the days of her life.","is_omitted":0,"source_line":2847},{"translation_id":"engwebu","book_id":"engwebu:pro","chapter":31,"verse_ordinal":897,"verse_start":13,"verse_end":13,"verse_label":"13","text":"She seeks wool and flax, and works eagerly with her hands.","is_omitted":0,"source_line":2850},{"translation_id":"engwebu","book_id":"engwebu:pro","chapter":31,"verse_ordinal":898,"verse_start":14,"verse_end":14,"verse_label":"14","text":"She is like the merchant ships. She brings her bread from afar.","is_omitted":0,"source_line":2853},{"translation_id":"engwebu","book_id":"engwebu:pro","chapter":31,"verse_ordinal":899,"verse_start":15,"verse_end":15,"verse_label":"15","text":"She rises also while it is yet night, gives food to her household, and portions for her servant girls.","is_omitted":0,"source_line":2856},{"translation_id":"engwebu","book_id":"engwebu:pro","chapter":31,"verse_ordinal":900,"verse_start":16,"verse_end":16,"verse_label":"16","text":"She considers a field, and buys it. With the fruit of her hands, she plants a vineyard.","is_omitted":0,"source_line":2860},{"translation_id":"engwebu","book_id":"engwebu:pro","chapter":31,"verse_ordinal":901,"verse_start":17,"verse_end":17,"verse_label":"17","text":"She arms her waist with strength, and makes her arms strong.","is_omitted":0,"source_line":2863},{"translation_id":"engwebu","book_id":"engwebu:pro","chapter":31,"verse_ordinal":902,"verse_start":18,"verse_end":18,"verse_label":"18","text":"She perceives that her merchandise is profitable. Her lamp doesn’t go out by night.","is_omitted":0,"source_line":2866},{"translation_id":"engwebu","book_id":"engwebu:pro","chapter":31,"verse_ordinal":903,"verse_start":19,"verse_end":19,"verse_label":"19","text":"She lays her hands to the distaff, and her hands hold the spindle.","is_omitted":0,"source_line":2869},{"translation_id":"engwebu","book_id":"engwebu:pro","chapter":31,"verse_ordinal":904,"verse_start":20,"verse_end":20,"verse_label":"20","text":"She opens her arms to the poor; yes, she extends her hands to the needy.","is_omitted":0,"source_line":2872},{"translation_id":"engwebu","book_id":"engwebu:pro","chapter":31,"verse_ordinal":905,"verse_start":21,"verse_end":21,"verse_label":"21","text":"She is not afraid of the snow for her household, for all her household are clothed with scarlet.","is_omitted":0,"source_line":2875},{"translation_id":"engwebu","book_id":"engwebu:pro","chapter":31,"verse_ordinal":906,"verse_start":22,"verse_end":22,"verse_label":"22","text":"She makes for herself carpets of tapestry. Her clothing is fine linen and purple.","is_omitted":0,"source_line":2878},{"translation_id":"engwebu","book_id":"engwebu:pro","chapter":31,"verse_ordinal":907,"verse_start":23,"verse_end":23,"verse_label":"23","text":"Her husband is respected in the gates, when he sits among the elders of the land.","is_omitted":0,"source_line":2881},{"translation_id":"engwebu","book_id":"engwebu:pro","chapter":31,"verse_ordinal":908,"verse_start":24,"verse_end":24,"verse_label":"24","text":"She makes linen garments and sells them, and delivers sashes to the merchant.","is_omitted":0,"source_line":2884},{"translation_id":"engwebu","book_id":"engwebu:pro","chapter":31,"verse_ordinal":909,"verse_start":25,"verse_end":25,"verse_label":"25","text":"Strength and dignity are her clothing. She laughs at the time to come.","is_omitted":0,"source_line":2887},{"translation_id":"engwebu","book_id":"engwebu:pro","chapter":31,"verse_ordinal":910,"verse_start":26,"verse_end":26,"verse_label":"26","text":"She opens her mouth with wisdom. Kind instruction is on her tongue.","is_omitted":0,"source_line":2890},{"translation_id":"engwebu","book_id":"engwebu:pro","chapter":31,"verse_ordinal":911,"verse_start":27,"verse_end":27,"verse_label":"27","text":"She looks well to the ways of her household, and doesn’t eat the bread of idleness.","is_omitted":0,"source_line":2893},{"translation_id":"engwebu","book_id":"engwebu:pro","chapter":31,"verse_ordinal":912,"verse_start":28,"verse_end":28,"verse_label":"28","text":"Her children rise up and call her blessed. Her husband also praises her:","is_omitted":0,"source_line":2896},{"translation_id":"engwebu","book_id":"engwebu:pro","chapter":31,"verse_ordinal":913,"verse_start":29,"verse_end":29,"verse_label":"29","text":"“Many women do noble things, but you excel them all.”","is_omitted":0,"source_line":2899},{"translation_id":"engwebu","book_id":"engwebu:pro","chapter":31,"verse_ordinal":914,"verse_start":30,"verse_end":30,"verse_label":"30","text":"Charm is deceitful, and beauty is vain; but a woman who fears the LORD, she shall be praised.","is_omitted":0,"source_line":2902},{"translation_id":"engwebu","book_id":"engwebu:pro","chapter":31,"verse_ordinal":915,"verse_start":31,"verse_end":31,"verse_label":"31","text":"Give her of the fruit of her hands! Let her works praise her in the gates!","is_omitted":0,"source_line":2905}]}